 "help-flag": {
  "argv": [
   "--help"
  ],
  "cwd": "plain",
  "env": {},
  "exit": 0,
  "reply": [
   200,
   {
    "ok": true,
    "value": {}
   }
  ],
  "requests": [],
  "stderr": "",
  "stdout": "pulsar-msg \u2014 message another pulse (wakes it if stopped).\n\n  pulsar-msg <target_pulse_id> \"the text\"\n  pulsar-msg <target_pulse_id> < report.md        # text from stdin\n  pulsar-msg --from <my_id> <target_pulse_id> \"...\"\n\nThe sender id (from_pulse_id) is taken from the cwd (pulses run in\n<data>/pulses/<id>/cli), then $PULSAR_PULSE_ID, or --from. The target sees\n\"[message from 'Your title' (pulse <your id>)] the text\". Find ids with\npulsar-roster --grep <title>. Any apostrophes, quotes, parentheses or\nnewlines in the text are fine: the JSON is built here, not in your shell.\n"
 },
